      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LAMBRO LOUELLA (4) was ultra impressive when she led from one spot wider and cruised home by a whopping 36m at this circuit and distance last week, making it three wins on the trot. Should push forward again and looks tough to catch. Stablemate WITHA BITTA LUCK (3) is yet to taste defeat, spanking her rivals on debut before leading to take out her heat by 1.3m here last week. Should push forward again so could challenge her barn mate. Emma Stewart's KENZINGTON (2) is the query runner. She started a hot favourite on debut in the heats but broke and wound up third. Suspect there is ability there so can improve plenty if she gets it right. MY ROCKING HORSE (5) is next best after her solid second to WITHA BITTA LUCK last week.",
